1
00:00:03,280 --> 00:00:05,380
我终于来到了这里
Oh, I'm finally here.

2
00:00:05,560 --> 00:00:06,539
这一直是我的梦想
Oh, this has been my dream

3
00:00:06,539 --> 00:00:08,412
从我看过《一个美国人在巴黎》后就如此了
ever since I saw "An American in Paris."

4
00:00:08,412 --> 00:00:09,620
影响我的电影是《天使爱美丽》
For me, it was "Amélie."

5
00:00:09,620 --> 00:00:11,079
我当年还强迫我妈给我剪女主同款发型
I made my mom give me that haircut.

6
00:00:11,079 --> 00:00:13,164
情人节快乐 宝贝
Happy Valentine's Day, mon cheri.

7
00:00:13,529 --> 00:00:15,083
基佬巴黎[美好巴黎]
Ah, gay Paree.

8
00:00:15,083 --> 00:00:16,480
瞧 我就说克莱尔肯定会用这个哏吐槽
See, I told you it would be Claire.

9
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:17,580
我押的是杰会吐槽
I had my money on Jay.

10
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:18,600
抱歉 姑娘们
Sorry, ladies,

11
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:19,800
我心情太好不想吐槽
I'm in too good a mood.

12
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,080
没什么大事
It's no big deal.

13
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:23,020
我只是在今年的国际衣柜博览会上
I'm getting a lifetime achievement award

14
00:00:23,020 --> 00:00:26,240
获得了终身成就奖
at this year's Expo Internationale du Closet.

15
00:00:26,680 --> 00:00:28,820
他们怎么不把最后一个词也翻成法语
Why don't they translate the last word?

16
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:31,200
我相信法语里肯定有"衣柜"这个词吧
I'm sure they have a word for closet.

17
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:32,020
他们是法国人
They're French.

18
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:34,440
或许是没翻到最后一个词 就习惯性罢工了
Maybe they went on strike before they got to the end.

19
00:00:34,544 --> 00:00:39,120
普里契特先生 欢迎来到皇冠广场酒店
Monsieur Pritchett, welcome to the Crowne Plaza.

20
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:40,400
我是伯纳德·布斯
I am Bernard Busse,

21
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:43,200
国际衣柜行会的主席
president of the International Closet Guild.

22
00:00:43,708 --> 00:00:44,685
么么
Mwah!

23
00:00:44,913 --> 00:00:45,780
么么
Mwah!

24
00:00:45,780 --> 00:00:47,200
老天 他还发出恶心的声音
Oh, God. He made the sound.

25
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:50,500
这位女士根本无需介绍
And this woman needs no introduction.

26
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:54,320
你跟杰在邮件中形容的一样美
You are just as beautiful as Jay described in his e-mail.

27
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,240
很高兴见到你 斯黛拉
It's a pleasure to meet you, Stella.

28
00:00:57,240 --> 00:00:59,550
不 不 这是我妻子歌洛莉亚
Oh, no, no. This is my wife, Gloria.

29
00:00:59,550 --> 00:01:02,060
我本来想在邮件中提到你的 但一写就太长了
I-I put you in the e-mail, but then it was too long.

30
00:01:02,820 --> 00:01:06,760
希望在一小时后的鸡尾酒招待会上见到二位
I hope to see you both at the cocktail reception in an hour.

31
00:01:07,512 --> 00:01:08,802
待会儿见
A bientot.

32
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:09,975
再见[西语]
Adios.

33
00:01:09,975 --> 00:01:12,400
你可真会乱上添乱 还掺杂第三种语言
'Cause that's what we need. A third language.

34
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:14,020
我们有一小时的时间 去观光吧
We have an hour. We should go sightseeing.

35
00:01:14,140 --> 00:01:15,700
-或许去看看巴黎圣母院 -不了 谢谢
- Maybe check out Notre Dame. - No, thank you.

36
00:01:15,780 --> 00:01:16,920
我曾见过它辉煌的样子
I saw it back in the day,

37
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:18,240
而非如今这般空有壳没有魂
before it was a shell of itself.

38
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:20,000
再去看一次 只会让我郁闷难受
Seeing it again would only depress me.

39
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:21,200
是啊 我懂你的意思
Yeah, I know what you mean.

40
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:22,976
所以我现在都没法去西尔斯百货购物了[实则已破产倒闭]
That's why I can't shop at Sears.

41
00:01:22,976 --> 00:01:25,240
曼尼 你去帮我们办理登记入住吧
Manny, why don't you go and check us in

42
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:27,020
因为你让整个家族蒙羞
since you disgraced this family

43
00:01:27,020 --> 00:01:29,500
你竟然学法语 而不是西班牙语
by learning French instead of Spanish.

44
00:01:29,620 --> 00:01:31,580
一定要拿下他们承诺我的那个房间
And get that room that they promised me.

45
00:01:31,980 --> 00:01:33,800
显然某个伯爵曾在那里睡过
Apparently some earl once slept there.

46
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:35,220
我们太为你骄傲了 爸
We're so proud of you, Dad.

47
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:38,100
谢谢 我只希望我父亲能在此看到这一幕
Thanks. I only wish my old man could be here to see this.

48
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:38,740
说起来也好笑
You know, it's funny.

49
00:01:39,160 --> 00:01:41,040
他参与过诺曼底登陆战
He stormed the beaches of Normandy,

50
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:42,780
我却要领取衣柜界的大奖了
and I'm getting a closet award.

51
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:44,040
后辈不断超越祖辈的光辉
We keep topping each other.

52
00:01:44,120 --> 00:01:45,300
谁知道小乔能有怎样伟大的成就呢
Who knows what Joe will do?

53
00:01:46,571 --> 00:01:48,120
你有什么安排
Hey, w-what are you doing now?

54
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:50,000
你懂的 情人节嘛
Well, you know, it's Valentine's Day,

55
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,120
所以我打算跟我丈夫一起
so I think I'm gonna enjoy

56
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:53,680
享受这世上最浪漫的城市
the most romantic city in the world with my husband.

57
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:55,900
抱歉
Sorry.

58
00:01:56,820 --> 00:01:59,240
菲尔去不成巴黎 因为他有工作要忙
Phil can't come to Paris because he has to work.

59
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:02,720
虽然很扫兴 但我一个人也会玩得很开心
It stinks, but I am still gonna have so much fun

60
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:04,020
因为我打算重游
visiting all my favorite places

61
00:02:04,020 --> 00:02:05,840
当年在那里短期留学时最爱的地方
from the semester I spent there in college.

62
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:07,080
房地产紧急事件
Real-estate emergency.

63
00:02:07,205 --> 00:02:09,189
经纪人和客户间的保密协议
Um, broker/client confidentiality

64
00:02:09,189 --> 00:02:10,933
禁止我谈论具体事宜
fobids me from discussing it.

65
00:02:11,100 --> 00:02:12,180
我见过的那些事...
The stuff I've seen...

66
00:02:12,180 --> 00:02:13,280
你们不会想知道的
You do not want to know.

67
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:14,440
没错
Correct.

68
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:15,940
如果你愿意
Look, if you want,

69
00:02:15,960 --> 00:02:19,860
并且当电灯泡也不会让你觉得太尴尬 或许...
and you don't feel too awkward about being a third wheel, maybe --

70
00:02:20,243 --> 00:02:21,820
米奇尔竟因可怜我而相邀
Pity invite from Mitchell?

71
00:02:21,820 --> 00:02:23,836
真是风水轮流转啊
How the tables have turned.

72
00:02:23,836 --> 00:02:24,720
不了 谢谢
No, merci.

73
00:02:24,720 --> 00:02:26,540
我要去找我最爱的咖啡厅
I'm gonna go find my favorite cafe,

74
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:29,320
喝一杯葡萄酒 不为自己独自一人而伤悲
have a glass of wine, and try not to be sad that I'm all alone.

75
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:30,300
好吧 祝你玩得开心
Okay, great. Have fun.

76
00:02:30,660 --> 00:02:31,100
再见
Bye.

77
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:49,460
我听说这里的面包
You know, I heard the bread here

78
00:02:49,460 --> 00:02:51,037
比我们国家的那种要健康些
is healthier than the kind we have back home.

79
00:02:51,037 --> 00:02:52,760
那怎么可能呢 面包就是面包啊
Well, how is that possible? Bread is bread.

80
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:56,022
按常理是这样 但实际上这里的谷物...
You would think, but it's actually the way that the grain is, um --

81
00:02:56,022 --> 00:02:58,554
不对 是因为烤箱...
No, no, it's -- It's the way that the -- the ovens --

82
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:01,200
好吧 反正我要趁在这里吃很多面包
Okay, look, I'm gonna have a lot of bread while we're here.

83
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:02,120
它们必须得好
I need it to be okay.

84
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:04,220
我真的很抱歉
I am so sorry.

85
00:03:04,820 --> 00:03:05,680
我好像有点倒不过来时差
I think I'm jet-lagged.

86
00:03:05,680 --> 00:03:06,780
不如这样吧 我去睡个觉
You know what? I might take a nap

87
00:03:06,780 --> 00:03:09,360
你自己出去游玩探索吧
while you go out and explore.

88
00:03:10,454 --> 00:03:12,900
是什么声音啊 你的箱子怎么会发出声响
What was that? W-Why did your bag honk?

89
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:15,000
可能是电话声吧 这里的电话铃声都是那种的
I think that was a phone. You know, that's how they ring here.

90
00:03:15,522 --> 00:03:17,160
谁快接一下电话啊 有人吗 快
Will somebody answer that? Hmm? Hmm?

91
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:19,060
别生气
Don't be mad.

92
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:20,060
菲茨宝
Fizbo?

93
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:22,980
你说你的箱子装不下我的毛衣
My sweaters were too bulky to pack,

94
00:03:22,980 --> 00:03:24,060
但却能装得下菲茨宝装备
but Fizbo made the cut?

95
00:03:24,160 --> 00:03:26,240
拜托 你知道我一直以来都有一个梦想
Oh, come on. You know it's always been my dream to --

96
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:28,596
就是将菲茨宝的魔力带到法国街头
to bring the magic of Fizbo to the streets of Paris.

97
00:03:28,720 --> 00:03:29,820
你并不是倒不过来时差
You're not jet-lagged.

98
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:32,500
你是打算偷偷溜出去 在街上"丑来丑去"
You were gonna sneak out and go clown around.

99
00:03:32,660 --> 00:03:34,437
你知道这个说法不对 是"扮小丑逗乐"
You know that's not how we say it. It's "Clown about."

100
00:03:34,437 --> 00:03:35,900
我真不敢相信你竟然对我撒谎了
I-I can't believe you lied to me.

101
00:03:35,900 --> 00:03:37,340
我也不敢相信我还得对你撒谎才行
Well, I can't believe I had to.

102
00:03:37,420 --> 00:03:39,720
大多数小丑的配偶都是非常支持他们的
You know, most clowns have spouses that are supportive.

103
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:42,240
我才不信大多数小丑能有配偶
I'm not convinced most clowns have spouses.

104
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:47,000
克莱尔即将见到
Claire was about to meet

105
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,820
克莱夫·比克斯比的法国表哥 克劳德
Clive Bixby's French cousin, Claude.

106
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:51,500
计划很简单
The plan was simple enough.

107
00:03:51,580 --> 00:03:53,420
我只需捏造一个工作上的紧急事件
All I did was create a fake work emergency

108
00:03:53,420 --> 00:03:54,960
然后在克莱尔最爱的咖啡厅等她
and wait for Claire at her favorite cafe.

109
00:03:56,300 --> 00:03:59,120
欢迎来到法国 请问您本次来的目的是
Welcome to France. What is the purpose of your visit?

110
00:03:59,630 --> 00:04:00,820
爱情
L'amour.

111
00:04:00,820 --> 00:04:02,232
先生 请老实回答问题
Just answer the question, sir!

112
00:04:02,232 --> 00:04:03,600
抱歉抱歉
Oh, I'm s-so sorry.

113
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:04,540
来办事...
Um, business...

114
00:04:05,187 --> 00:04:06,532
办情事
of l'amour.

115
00:04:15,900 --> 00:04:17,900
加点糖会顺口一点
It helps to add a little sugar...

116
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:18,680
克劳德兄
Claude.

117
00:04:18,858 --> 00:04:20,452
谢谢 但其实...
Oh. Thank you, but th--

118
00:04:20,452 --> 00:04:22,540
这个... 不是我的真名
this is, uh, not my real name.

119
00:04:22,540 --> 00:04:24,260
是我的情圣第二人格
It's my romantic alter ego.

120
00:04:25,020 --> 00:04:26,500
我是来给我老婆一个惊喜
I'm surprising my wife.

121
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:27,660
不错哦
Not bad.

122
00:04:27,660 --> 00:04:28,740
以美国人的标准来说
For an American.

123
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:30,380
是吗 你能做到比我更深情吗
Oh, really? You can do better?

124
00:04:32,180 --> 00:04:35,780
许多年以前 我在这间咖啡厅遇到一个女孩
Many years ago, I met a woman in this very cafe.

125
00:04:35,780 --> 00:04:39,260
我们有过短暂但激烈的一段情缘
We had a brief but passionate affair,

126
00:04:39,820 --> 00:04:41,320
白天我们一同探访了巴黎各处
spending our days exploring Paris

127
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:43,000
而在晚上
and our nights...

128
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,700
我们也探索对方身体各处
exploring each other.

129
00:04:46,391 --> 00:04:47,740
我有一次曾带一个女人
Well, I-I once took a woman

130
00:04:47,740 --> 00:04:50,020
去了迪士尼乐园与诺式莓果乐园
to both Disneyland and Knott's Berry Farm.

131
00:04:50,020 --> 00:04:52,160
在同一天内
In the same day.

132
00:04:53,531 --> 00:04:54,885
在我们分开的那一天
On the day we parted...

133
00:04:55,880 --> 00:05:00,460
我们约定好会在这个情人节在此相见
we promised to meet here on this Valentine's Day

134
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:02,520
来重燃我们的爱火
to rekindle our love.

135
00:05:02,740 --> 00:05:03,240
但谁知道呢
Who knows?

136
00:05:04,026 --> 00:05:06,488
她记得这件事的几率非常...
The chances of her even remembering --

137
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:07,760
偶买噶
Oh, mon dieu.

138
00:05:09,097 --> 00:05:10,231
-克莱尔 -克莱尔
- Claire! - Claire!

139
00:05:14,760 --> 00:05:15,320
你好
Bonjour.

140
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:16,440
哈喽
Hello.

141
00:05:18,444 --> 00:05:19,806
骚瑞 对不起
I'm -- I'm so sorry.

142
00:05:19,868 --> 00:05:22,154
"骚瑞" 你怎么知道我懂英语呢
"Sorry"? H-How did you know I speak English?

143
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:23,800
祝您旅途愉快
Have a nice visit.

144
00:05:27,520 --> 00:05:28,080
不好意西
Excusez-moi.

145
00:05:29,094 --> 00:05:31,260
宰哪李...
Um... ou se trouve, um...

146
00:05:31,260 --> 00:05:32,540
你想要去哪里
What are you looking for?

147
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:34,320
看蒙娜丽莎 去麦当劳
Mona Lisa? McDonald's?

148
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:35,551
都在那个方向
Both are that way.

149
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:38,220
先提醒你 我们法国这里餐点都是正常大小
Heads up, the portions here are normal-size.

150
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:40,980
你怎么知道我是美国人 我的口音有那么蹩脚吗
H-How did you know I'm American? Is my accent that bad?

151
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:45,140
我们穿着一样啊
We're dressed the same.

152
00:05:45,380 --> 00:05:47,540
没需要这么人身攻击我吧
There's no reason to attack me.

153
00:05:54,700 --> 00:05:56,080
杰在哪里
Hey. Where's Jay?

154
00:05:56,340 --> 00:05:57,500
我觉得他好像紧张了
I think he's nervous.

155
00:05:57,700 --> 00:06:00,180
他已经换了三次衣服
He has changed his outfit three times.

156
00:06:00,180 --> 00:06:03,540
如果娶我的体验也是这样 那还真是不容易
If this is what it's like to be married to me, it's no picnic.

157
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:04,420
我们有个麻烦
We have a problem.

158
00:06:04,540 --> 00:06:06,920
我得带你看个东西 跟我来
I have to show you something. Come here.

159
00:06:08,424 --> 00:06:09,780
波尔·桑德斯
Burl Saunders!

160
00:06:09,780 --> 00:06:11,260
很接近了 是厄尔·钱伯斯
Close. Earl Chambers.

161
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:13,020
得奖的人不是杰
Jay isn't getting the award.

162
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:15,440
他是来替他的前搭档厄尔领奖的人
He's accepting it on behalf of his ex-partner, Earl.

163
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:15,960
什么
What?

164
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:17,440
怎么会这样
How?

165
00:06:17,980 --> 00:06:19,080
当博览会打来的时候
When the Expo called,

166
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:21,420
是曼尼负责跟他们交流的 因为他会说法语
Manny talked to them because he speaks French.

167
00:06:21,780 --> 00:06:23,780
至少当时他是这么觉得的
At least, he thought he did.

168
00:06:23,980 --> 00:06:26,440
我想解释 是因为法语的"酒店房间"
In my defense, the French word for "Hotel room"

169
00:06:26,440 --> 00:06:27,520
听起来跟"钱伯"很像
sounds a lot like "Chamber."

170
00:06:27,561 --> 00:06:29,252
是 是
Oh, oui, oui.

171
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:31,620
他们说要让你们住总统套房
They said you're putting you up in the royal suite.

172
00:06:31,880 --> 00:06:33,180
以前好像是某个伯爵[厄尔]的房间
It used to be some earl's chamber.

173
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:35,820
我们衣柜界的人就是这样 格调就是高
That's closet people for you -- class all the way!

174
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:38,500
他来了 我们怎么做
Ah. He's here. What do we do?

175
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:40,420
什么都不做 跟他说实话
Nothing. Tell him the truth.

176
00:06:40,700 --> 00:06:42,800
杰是个成年人了 他能承受
Jay's a grown man. He can handle it.

177
00:06:42,960 --> 00:06:44,280
行 但如果他朝我喉咙攻过来了
Okay, but if he goes for my throat,

178
00:06:44,280 --> 00:06:46,254
准备好打给"走 妖 妖"吧
be ready to dial neuf, un, un.

179
00:06:46,254 --> 00:06:49,489
这个语言 就像是一群马在讲话
That language. It's like a bunch of horses talking.

180
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:53,940
看看这里 该来的都来了
Look at this place. Everybody's here.

181
00:06:54,059 --> 00:06:56,861
柏林衣柜局的海因里希·穆勒
Heinrich Muler of Berlin Closet-stadt,

182
00:06:56,861 --> 00:07:00,560
东京衣柜与罐装鲸鱼肉的苏珊·贞树
Susan Sadaki from Tokyo Closets and Canned Whale Meat.

183
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:01,720
衣柜界有头有脸的都来了
It's a regular who's who.

184
00:07:01,900 --> 00:07:03,820
是啊 哪怕你说出了他们的名字 我还是对不上
Yeah, even when you say all their names.

185
00:07:04,020 --> 00:07:05,040
我必须跟你说
You know, I gotta tell you,

186
00:07:05,100 --> 00:07:07,140
这个奖真的是来得太及时了
this award couldn't have come at a better time.

187
00:07:07,300 --> 00:07:10,260
在我失去衣柜公司后 有时我觉得
With my closet company gone, sometimes it feels like

188
00:07:10,260 --> 00:07:12,520
我这一生并没有足以展现给人看的成就
I don't have anything to show for a lifetime of work,

189
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:13,460
仿佛我做过的一切都无足轻重
like it didn't matter.

190
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:14,920
但受到肯定我就知道不是了
But now I know it did.

191
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:16,240
是的
Yes.

192
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:17,740
在这里等我
Wait here.

193
00:07:17,940 --> 00:07:19,200
我马上回来
I'll be right back.

194
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:24,397
新计划 我要带他离开这里 我吸引他注意
New plan -- I'm getting him out of here, keeping him busy.

195
00:07:24,397 --> 00:07:26,920
你去跟衣柜界的人谈
You go and talk to the closet people.

196
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:28,760
让他们把奖颁给他
Make them give him an award.

197
00:07:29,140 --> 00:07:31,720
任何奖都行 他不会知道有何区别
Any kind of award. He won't know the difference.

198
00:07:31,900 --> 00:07:33,240
-怎么做到 -贿赂啊
- How? - Bribe them.

199
00:07:33,300 --> 00:07:35,300
黒函恐吓啊 色诱啊
Blackmail them. Seduce them.

200
00:07:35,340 --> 00:07:36,820
我是没把你教好吗
Have I taught you nothing.

201
00:07:39,520 --> 00:07:41,027
-菲尔 -克莱尔
- Phil? - Claire.

202
00:07:41,027 --> 00:07:42,600
-克莱尔 -基
- Claire? - Guy?

203
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:45,302
天啊 你怎么会在这里
Oh, my God. What are you doing here?

204
00:07:45,302 --> 00:07:46,527
克莱尔 你认识这"基"友吗
Claire, you know this Guy?

205
00:07:46,840 --> 00:07:48,660
以前认识的啦
Well, um...I used to.

206
00:07:49,540 --> 00:07:51,920
你们两个在这里做什么呢
What are you both doing here?

207
00:07:52,220 --> 00:07:54,180
我来给你个情人节惊喜啊
I came to surprise you on Valentine's Day.

208
00:07:54,500 --> 00:07:56,041
你记得你飞机上那个满脸绷带的人吗
You know the guy on the plane with all the face bandages?

209
00:07:56,041 --> 00:07:56,836
那个人是我
That was me.

210
00:07:57,900 --> 00:07:59,560
克莱尔 你难道忘了
Claire, do you not remember

211
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:01,800
你30年前跟我约好要在今日
asking me to meet you here in this cafe

212
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:04,180
在这个咖啡厅见面吗
exactly 30 years after we parted?

213
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:05,000
隐隐约约吧
Vaguely.

214
00:08:05,880 --> 00:08:08,260
我真是疯了才会认为我有希望
I-I-I was crazy to think this could work out.

215
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:12,060
你这么美好的女人当然早就结婚了
Of course a woman as magnificent as you is married.

216
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:16,660
我并不想打扰你们浪漫的一天
I don't want to interfere with your day of romance.

217
00:08:16,660 --> 00:08:18,960
我会独自一个人在我们的老地点徘徊
I will wander our old haunts alone

218
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:21,120
然后回我的酒店去
and return to my hotel

219
00:08:21,120 --> 00:08:23,400
让如影随形的回忆将我包裹
in the ghostly embrace of our memories.

220
00:08:24,404 --> 00:08:26,257
-再会 克莱尔 -行了 再见
- Adieu, Claire. - Okay, cool. Bye.

221
00:08:26,257 --> 00:08:27,697
-是啊 -我们走
- Yeah. - Let's go.

222
00:08:29,995 --> 00:08:32,780
好了 大日子 满满的日程
Alright, big day. Lots of plans.

223
00:08:32,780 --> 00:08:35,820
第一件事 进入角色
First things first, getting into character.

224
00:08:37,020 --> 00:08:37,700
克劳德·比克斯比
Claude Bixby,

225
00:08:38,131 --> 00:08:40,484
芥末大亨 天赋异禀
mustard magnate with a flair for --

226
00:08:40,484 --> 00:08:42,657
菲尔 克劳德
Uh, Phil -- Claude --

227
00:08:42,657 --> 00:08:44,840
你这样大费周章我很开心
I-I love that you're doing all of this,

228
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:46,600
但就这样甩掉基
but doesn't some tiny part of you

229
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:48,480
你心里没有一点内疚吗
feel guilty for ditching Guy?

230
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:54,119
他都等了我30年呢
I mean, he did wait for me for 30 years.

231
00:08:54,119 --> 00:08:55,962
我们可以邀请他一起喝杯红酒
We could invite him for a glass of wine.

232
00:08:57,180 --> 00:08:57,660
好吧
Fine.

233
00:08:58,040 --> 00:09:00,240
但我警告你 假如他越界
But I'm warning you, if he gets out of line,

234
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:01,600
克劳德会空手道
Claude knows karate.

235
00:09:01,620 --> 00:09:04,616
还会以色列格斗术 他母亲是犹太血统
And Krav Maga. He's Jewish on his mother's side.

236
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:08,000
我们往这边走 去博物馆
Let's go this way, to the museum.

237
00:09:08,100 --> 00:09:08,840
你确定吗
Are you sure?

238
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:10,980
我觉得他们在等我回去
I think they're expecting me back inside.

239
00:09:11,280 --> 00:09:12,340
让他们等
Make them wait.

240
00:09:12,340 --> 00:09:15,780
你以为新娘为什么都最后入场
Why do you think the brides arrive after everyone else?

241
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:17,040
你就是新娘
You're the bride.

242
00:09:17,180 --> 00:09:18,196
是啊 我是新娘
Yeah, I'm the bride.

243
00:09:18,196 --> 00:09:19,840
-那好 我们 -不不不
- Alright, let's -- - No, no, no.

244
00:09:19,840 --> 00:09:20,956
其实是这边
You know what? It's this side.

245
00:09:20,956 --> 00:09:21,960
-明天 -不
- So, tomorrow -- - No, no!

246
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:24,540
抱歉 其实是这边
You know what? I'm sorry. It's this way.

247
00:09:24,960 --> 00:09:26,700
逗我玩吗
Are you kidding me?!

248
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:27,160
怎么了
What?!

249
00:09:27,580 --> 00:09:29,040
太美了
How beautiful!

250
00:09:34,340 --> 00:09:34,820
你好
Bonjour.

251
00:09:34,910 --> 00:09:35,326
你好
B-Bonjour.

252
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:38,640
你好
Bonjour.

253
00:09:42,060 --> 00:09:43,535
抱歉 不好意思
Pardon. Excusez-moi.

254
00:09:50,660 --> 00:09:51,140
你好
Bonjour.

255
00:09:52,080 --> 00:09:53,280
一位吗 先生
Une table pour un, monsieur?

256
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:01,880
克莱尔 还记得那次
Oh, Claire, remember that time

257
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:04,020
我们溜进了那家葡萄酒吧的酒窖
when we snuck into the cellar of that wine bar?

258
00:10:04,180 --> 00:10:06,960
天哪 那时我们是那么年轻疯狂
Oh, God, we were so crazy and so young!

259
00:10:06,960 --> 00:10:08,580
现在可不是了 你说什么 外婆
Not anymore. What's that, Grandma?

260
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:09,580
她已经当外婆了
She's a grandma now.

261
00:10:11,020 --> 00:10:14,080
没有比生命创造生命更美的事了
Well, there's nothing more beautiful than a life creating life,

262
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:15,500
-反过来讲 -创造更多生命
- which in turn -- - Creates more life.

263
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:19,040
克莱尔和我该走了
Well, uh...Claire and I should get going.

264
00:10:19,293 --> 00:10:21,000
我还想去圣心大教堂
I was hoping to get up to Sacre Coeur

265
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,340
眺望整座城市
to get a view of the whole city.

266
00:10:22,680 --> 00:10:23,140
没必要
No need.

267
00:10:23,640 --> 00:10:25,860
我在半岛酒店有露台花园套房
I have a rooftop garden suite at The Peninsula.

268
00:10:26,120 --> 00:10:27,380
有全市最好的风景
It's the best view in town.

269
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:29,260
这太完美了
How perfect is this?

270
00:10:30,420 --> 00:10:30,940
完美得令人泄气
Frustratingly!

271
00:10:32,196 --> 00:10:34,126
好了 开始吧
Alright. Here we go.

272
00:10:34,396 --> 00:10:35,974
让我看看
Let's see here.

273
00:10:38,194 --> 00:10:39,180
你好
Bonjour.

274
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:41,480
几分钟后我会在广场表演
In a few minutes, I'm going to be performing in the square.

275
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:44,023
我叫菲茨宝
Je m'appelle Fizbo.

276
00:10:46,799 --> 00:10:48,572
他才是菲茨宝
Lui, c'est Fizbeau.

277
00:10:48,603 --> 00:10:50,659
-什么 -他才是菲茨宝
- What? - He is Fizbeau!

278
00:10:50,700 --> 00:10:52,554
菲茨宝 知道吗
Fizbeau, okay?

279
00:11:01,420 --> 00:11:04,500
基 套房太美了
Guy, this suite is so beautiful.

280
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:06,317
我记得上次我们在巴黎时
I think the last time we were in Paris,

281
00:11:06,317 --> 00:11:08,580
连一法郎都要共享
we had a franc between the two of us.

282
00:11:08,580 --> 00:11:10,180
老天 法郎又是哪个郎
Oh, God! Who's Frank?

283
00:11:10,780 --> 00:11:12,340
我在生意场上很走运
I've been lucky in business,

284
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:14,260
情场就不走运了
less so in love.

285
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:17,240
我想我都因此变成工作狂了
I guess it's turned me into a workaholic.

286
00:11:17,620 --> 00:11:20,400
我每周肯定要在办公室十到十二个小时
I must be in the office 10, 12 hours a week.

287
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:22,815
要喝些香槟吗
Shall we have some champagne?

288
00:11:22,815 --> 00:11:24,240
不 谢了
Uh, no, thank you.

289
00:11:24,240 --> 00:11:25,760
我真的没心情喝香槟
I'm not really in the mood for champagne.

290
00:11:25,940 --> 00:11:27,880
那我们走运了 因为只有两个杯子
Lucky for us, because there are only two glasses.

291
00:11:29,660 --> 00:11:32,040
请允许我来敬酒
Allow me to make a toast.

292
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:34,140
敬菲尔
To Phil.

293
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:36,820
敬他允许我与你共度这一点时光
For allowing me to spend a bit more time

294
00:11:36,820 --> 00:11:38,498
我认识过的最慷慨的情人
with the most generous lover I've ever --

295
00:11:38,498 --> 00:11:40,720
好了 你的小把戏我都看穿了
Okay! I see what you're doing here.

296
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:43,760
香槟 酒店套房 旋转木马
The champagne, the hotel suite, that carousel ride.

297
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:47,137
每次我转过来你俩就不笑了
You two stopped laughing every time I circled around.

298
00:11:47,167 --> 00:11:48,891
抱歉 伙计 但这事没门
I'm sorry, buddy, but it's not gonna happen.

299
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:51,900
菲尔说得对 我已经结婚了
Phil's right. I'm a married woman.

300
00:11:51,900 --> 00:11:53,960
这个旅途不会有任何浪漫韵事
There will be no romance on this trip.

301
00:11:54,100 --> 00:11:56,318
抱歉 我真傻
I'm sorry. I've been a fool.

302
00:11:56,318 --> 00:11:59,960
看来我有点纵容自己沉醉于幻想之中了
I guess I let myself indulge in a fantasy more than I should.

303
00:12:00,140 --> 00:12:03,720
拜托 让我们假装这一切
Please, let us all pretend this...

304
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:05,040
从未发生过
never happened.

305
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:06,180
等等
Wait.

306
00:12:06,432 --> 00:12:08,665
你用了普朗克误导
Was that Poulanc's misdirect?

307
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:09,560
没错
Indeed.

308
00:12:11,442 --> 00:12:13,100
你也是魔术师吗
A fellow prestidigitator?

309
00:12:13,100 --> 00:12:13,740
是的
Yes!

310
00:12:14,620 --> 00:12:15,580
来握个手
Put her there.

311
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:18,700
您的手表 先生
Your watch, sir?

312
00:12:18,700 --> 00:12:19,860
-在找这个吗 -什么
- Looking for this? - What?!

313
00:12:19,940 --> 00:12:20,860
不可能
Oh, no way!

314
00:12:21,460 --> 00:12:22,520
我们该走了
We should bounce.

315
00:12:22,960 --> 00:12:24,980
告诉我 你们这次来一定会去
Tell me you're going to visit Le Musee des Magiciens

316
00:12:24,980 --> 00:12:25,673
魔术师博物馆
while you're here.

317
00:12:25,673 --> 00:12:26,940
魔术师博物馆
The Museum of Magicians?

318
00:12:26,940 --> 00:12:28,120
我想去想疯了 但他们在周五
I'm dying to go, but they're closed

319
00:12:28,120 --> 00:12:29,480
周六周日 还有周一周三
Fridays, Saturdays, and Sundays --

320
00:12:29,560 --> 00:12:30,900
都不开门
and Mondays and Wednesdays.

321
00:12:30,920 --> 00:12:32,340
认识馆长就能进去
Not if you know the owner.

322
00:12:32,540 --> 00:12:34,020
我能让我们进去私人参观
I can get us a private tour.

323
00:12:34,480 --> 00:12:34,920
太好了
Sweet!

324
00:12:35,220 --> 00:12:36,039
克莱尔 你怎么想
Claire, what do you say?

325
00:12:36,039 --> 00:12:37,560
我们可以假装把你锯成两半
We can pretend to saw you in half.

326
00:12:37,560 --> 00:12:38,560
或者真锯也行
Or just do it.

327
00:12:40,980 --> 00:12:42,680
你好 打扰一下
Hello. Hi. Hi. Excuse me.

328
00:12:42,740 --> 00:12:43,880
你为啥穿成这个样子
Why are you dressed like that?

329
00:12:43,880 --> 00:12:45,061
冒牌货
Imposteur!

330
00:12:45,061 --> 00:12:46,562
你是个冒牌货
Tu es un imposteur!

331
00:12:46,562 --> 00:12:48,102
你是 你才是个冒牌祸呢
You're -- You're the imposteur...

332
00:12:48,160 --> 00:12:50,115
如果这个词是我想的意思的话
if that word means what I think it means.

333
00:12:50,115 --> 00:12:51,520
他偷走了菲茨宝
He'd stolen Fizbo.

334
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:52,820
我迷之错落的彩格
The whimsically mismatched plaids,

335
00:12:52,900 --> 00:12:54,340
我标志性的一抹奔放腮红
my trademark bold splash of pink,

336
00:12:54,460 --> 00:12:55,120
还有我的蓝色嘴唇
my blue lip!

337
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:58,256
他很明显看过我网上的小丑教程
He'd clearly seen one of my online clown tutorials!

338
00:12:58,256 --> 00:13:00,020
各位 菲茨宝又和大家见面了
Hey, guys. Fizbo again.

339
00:13:00,020 --> 00:13:02,641
记得上腮红时要轻轻一扫
Just remember when you're applying your rouge to go easy.

340
00:13:02,641 --> 00:13:04,598
你是一个小丑 不是个荡妇
You're an Auguste clown, not a tramp.

341
00:13:05,260 --> 00:13:06,440
把外套给我
You know what? Give me the jacket.

342
00:13:06,620 --> 00:13:07,616
我
Oh! I --

343
00:13:07,866 --> 00:13:08,961
我应该想到的
I should've seen that coming.

344
00:13:08,961 --> 00:13:10,389
把你的手帕给我
Donne moi ce mouchoir!

345
00:13:14,347 --> 00:13:15,362
干得好啊 先生
Touche, monsieur!

346
00:13:15,362 --> 00:13:16,469
把我的假发还给我
You know what? Give me my wig.

347
00:13:17,874 --> 00:13:18,981
就在这时 我想起来[被它击中]了
And that's when it hit me.

348
00:13:21,100 --> 00:13:22,160
《欧洲小丑》
"The Clowns of Europe."

349
00:13:22,640 --> 00:13:24,320
我十几岁的时候买到的
I got this when I was a teenager.

350
00:13:24,375 --> 00:13:27,062
它就是我的青春
It was my "Sergeant Pepper's."

351
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:28,910
打开封皮 是一个又一个的小丑
Clown after clown pushing the envelope,

352
00:13:28,910 --> 00:13:31,118
包括菲茨寶
including Fizbeau.

353
00:13:31,118 --> 00:13:32,866
繁体寶
B-e-a-u!

354
00:13:33,540 --> 00:13:35,600
我还以为是我创造的角色 但他是对的
Here, I thought I'd come up with the idea, but he was right.

355
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:37,500
我才是冒牌祸
I was the imposteur.

356
00:13:37,640 --> 00:13:38,580
如果我没记错那个词的话
If that's the word.

357
00:13:38,580 --> 00:13:40,180
我高中的语言课
For my high school language requirement,

358
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:41,380
我选修了拍卖语言
I took auction-calling.

359
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:48,420
拿破仑的墓好壮观啊
See, isn't Napoleon's tomb spectacular?

360
00:13:48,660 --> 00:13:51,720
我先说好 我离世的时候不需要这些
Just so you know, when I go, I-I don't need all this.

361
00:13:53,420 --> 00:13:55,960
看 那不是曼尼吗
Look. That's Manny over there.

362
00:13:56,100 --> 00:13:56,500
不不
No, no.

363
00:13:56,500 --> 00:13:57,720
我去叫他
I'll go get him.

364
00:14:01,720 --> 00:14:02,900
怎么样
How did it go?

365
00:14:03,020 --> 00:14:04,440
他们会给杰颁奖吗
Are they giving Jay an award?

366
00:14:04,660 --> 00:14:07,320
不会 他们说这会开创一个不好的先例
No. They said it would set a very dangerous precedent.

367
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:08,660
用标准的英语说的
And in perfect English.

368
00:14:08,780 --> 00:14:10,040
看来这场蹩脚法语的误会
Turns out this whole misunderstanding

369
00:14:10,040 --> 00:14:11,200
本来是完全可以避免的
was completely avoidable.

370
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:12,820
我们得想个办法
We need to figure out something.

371
00:14:13,220 --> 00:14:14,900
可不能让杰发现
Jay can never find out

372
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:17,020
得奖的是厄尔而不是他
that Earl got an award instead of him.

373
00:14:19,180 --> 00:14:19,580
哇
Wow.

374
00:14:20,160 --> 00:14:21,120
看这里
Look at this place.

375
00:14:21,740 --> 00:14:23,360
这样的工艺 这样的建筑
The craftsmanship, the architecture.

376
00:14:23,700 --> 00:14:25,800
据说这个穹顶能起到耳语室的作用
They say the domed ceiling acts as a whisper chamber.

377
00:14:25,980 --> 00:14:27,500
耳语室是什么意思啊
What does "whisper chamber" mean?

378
00:14:28,160 --> 00:14:30,280
意思是我听到了你们刚刚说的
It means I heard everything you just said.

379
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:32,380
我平时得把电视机音量调高到40
I have to turn my TV up to 40,

380
00:14:32,420 --> 00:14:33,680
但你俩的对话是又清晰又响亮
but that was loud and clear!

381
00:14:44,596 --> 00:14:46,151
谢谢
Ah. Merci.

382
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:49,400
融入进去很简单嘛
It was easy to fit in.

383
00:14:49,460 --> 00:14:52,000
我要做的不过是穿好点 再装腔作势点
All I had to do was look good and have a lot of attitude.

384
00:14:52,400 --> 00:14:54,130
巴黎其实就像个巨大的同性恋酒吧
Paris was just like one big gay bar.

385
00:14:54,130 --> 00:14:55,301
来啦
Et voila.

386
00:14:58,936 --> 00:15:00,341
你的鸽子 先生
Votre pigeon, monsieur.

387
00:15:00,613 --> 00:15:01,588
"鸽子"
"Pigeon"?

388
00:15:02,046 --> 00:15:03,342
特色菜
Notre specialite.

389
00:15:03,342 --> 00:15:04,278
祝您有个好胃口
Ah. Bon appetit.

390
00:15:04,278 --> 00:15:05,108
好
Yah.

391
00:15:16,463 --> 00:15:17,740
不 我做不到
No. I can't -- I can't do it.

392
00:15:17,740 --> 00:15:19,697
我做不到 我不是法国人
I can't do it. I'm not French.

393
00:15:19,697 --> 00:15:21,713
我不吃这种东西
And I-I'm not eating that.

394
00:15:22,080 --> 00:15:23,940
这破围巾快逼疯我了
This scarf is driving me crazy!

395
00:15:25,643 --> 00:15:26,504
打扰一哈...
E-Excusez-moi --

396
00:15:26,504 --> 00:15:27,700
芝士汉堡在那边
Cheeseburger, that way.

397
00:15:27,700 --> 00:15:28,660
很棒 谢谢啦
Cool. Thanks, man!

398
00:15:32,180 --> 00:15:33,580
他们用那些古老的魔杖变出那么多魔术
It's amazing how much magic they got

399
00:15:33,580 --> 00:15:34,597
真是太让人震惊了
out of those old wands.

400
00:15:34,597 --> 00:15:37,280
现在 魔术师变魔术要简单多了
Today, magicians have it so easy, you know?

401
00:15:37,540 --> 00:15:38,520
是的
Oh, yeah.

402
00:15:38,595 --> 00:15:42,020
感觉到了分开的时刻了
Well, this basically feels like a natural breaking point,

403
00:15:42,020 --> 00:15:43,061
至少对我来说是
for me, at least.

404
00:15:43,061 --> 00:15:45,160
菲尔和我该 你懂的
Uh, Phil and I should probably you know?

405
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:46,798
当然 但我们的票
If you must, but our tickets

406
00:15:46,798 --> 00:15:49,320
也能让我们进自动化博物馆
also get us to Le Musee des Automates.

407
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:51,520
它们就像机器人 但非常初级的
They're like robots, but very primitive.

408
00:15:51,740 --> 00:15:53,200
基本上什么也不做
They basically do nothing.

409
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:56,300
就像我用汽车排烟管改造的那个吗
Um, like the one I built out of old mufflers?

410
00:15:56,460 --> 00:15:57,180
我们能去吗 克莱尔
Can we, Claire?

411
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:58,700
是啊 我们能去吗克莱尔
Oh, yes, can we, Claire?

412
00:15:59,820 --> 00:16:00,660
对不起
Excuse me.

413
00:16:01,380 --> 00:16:02,560
歌洛莉亚 怎么了
Hey, Gloria. What's up?

414
00:16:02,640 --> 00:16:03,660
我遇到难题了
I have a problem.

415
00:16:03,660 --> 00:16:04,960
我也是
Yeah, so do I.

416
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:06,360
才发现我貌似喜欢宅男
Apparently, I'm into nerds.

417
00:16:06,520 --> 00:16:07,300
是杰
It's Jay.

418
00:16:07,700 --> 00:16:09,440
得奖人不是他
He's not getting that award.

419
00:16:09,700 --> 00:16:10,100
什么
What?!

420
00:16:10,420 --> 00:16:12,281
是我们误会了
It was some kind of mistake,

421
00:16:12,281 --> 00:16:14,491
然后他发现这事 现在我们找不到他了
he found out, and now we can't find him.

422
00:16:14,491 --> 00:16:16,682
天啊 我马上过去
Oh, my God. Okay, I-I'll be right there.

423
00:16:16,740 --> 00:16:17,880
你确定没事吗
Are you sure it's okay?

424
00:16:18,119 --> 00:16:20,497
绝对没事
Uh, yeah, it's more than okay.

425
00:16:26,927 --> 00:16:28,287
你怎么找到我的
H-How did you find me?

426
00:16:28,360 --> 00:16:30,140
你穿得很显眼啊
Well, you're pretty easy to spot.

427
00:16:30,352 --> 00:16:32,840
对不起 我反应过度了
Look, I-I'm sorry I overreacted, okay?

428
00:16:32,840 --> 00:16:35,640
如果你想扮菲茨宝 那就扮菲茨宝吧
If you want to be Fizbo, be Fizbo.

429
00:16:35,860 --> 00:16:37,260
我再也不能扮菲茨宝了
I can never be Fizbo again.

430
00:16:37,840 --> 00:16:39,120
菲茨宝已死
Fizbo is dead.

431
00:16:39,360 --> 00:16:40,340
天啊 你这个人还真是善变
Oh, you're a moving target.

432
00:16:40,620 --> 00:16:43,080
我今天遇见正牌菲茨宝了
Look, I ran into the real Fizbo today,

433
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:44,820
他朝我脸上喷水
and he squirted me in the face with water

434
00:16:44,820 --> 00:16:46,000
还用书打我头了
and hit me in the head with a book.

435
00:16:46,100 --> 00:16:46,480
什么
What?!

436
00:16:47,380 --> 00:16:49,040
你看 我以为是我发明了
See, here, I thought I had created

437
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:50,180
这个奇妙独特的角色
this special, unique thing,

438
00:16:50,180 --> 00:16:52,760
但其实多年以来 我就是个剽窃的骗子
but I'm the one that's been a fraud all this time!

439
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:55,460
我要把这套小丑服扔河里
I'm throwing the suit in the river!

440
00:16:55,620 --> 00:16:56,020
等等
Wait.

441
00:16:56,820 --> 00:16:59,020
那样算乱丢垃圾 这边有垃圾桶
That's littering. There's a trash can right over here.

442
00:16:59,560 --> 00:16:59,960
等等啦
Wait!

443
00:17:00,070 --> 00:17:01,845
我必须要说...
Look, I-I gotta say, um --

444
00:17:02,314 --> 00:17:04,658
我不觉得你有剽窃任何东西
I don't -- I don't think you stole anything.

445
00:17:04,680 --> 00:17:05,420
你这是什么意思
What do you mean?

446
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:07,940
你看 你说他用书打了你的头
Well, you said he hit you in the head with a book.

447
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:09,820
但我以为菲茨宝只为人带来欢乐
I mean, I thought Fizbo was all about joy.

448
00:17:10,340 --> 00:17:12,660
是啊 他就是儿童般纯真的化身
He is. He's the embodiment of childlike innocence.

449
00:17:13,440 --> 00:17:13,500
这就对了
Exactly.

450
00:17:13,649 --> 00:17:16,162
-菲茨宝绝对不会使用暴力 -绝不
- Fizbo would never resort to violence. - Ever.

451
00:17:16,340 --> 00:17:18,680
那家伙感觉一点都不像菲茨宝
This guy doesn't sound like Fizbo to me.

452
00:17:18,822 --> 00:17:20,039
可是他看起来绝对是
Well, he sure looked like him.

453
00:17:20,039 --> 00:17:22,705
菲茨宝绝对不只是鞋子特大号
Fizbo's more than just a-a pair of big shoes

454
00:17:22,705 --> 00:17:24,956
还穿着完全不性感夹克的人
and an...un-sexy jacket.

455
00:17:24,956 --> 00:17:26,377
他是一种思想
He -- He's an idea.

456
00:17:26,700 --> 00:17:28,120
我今天学到的一件事
If I've learned anything today,

457
00:17:28,120 --> 00:17:30,200
那就是造就人的不是衣装
it's that clothes do not make the man...

458
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:31,400
衣装也不造就小丑
or the clown.

459
00:17:32,080 --> 00:17:34,540
你才是真正的菲茨宝
And you are the real Fizbo.

460
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:36,360
你是真心的吗
You mean it?

461
00:17:36,620 --> 00:17:37,460
事实就是如此
I know.

462
00:17:37,460 --> 00:17:38,940
走嘛
Now, come on.

463
00:17:38,960 --> 00:17:41,140
我们一起去享受巴黎 今天可是情人节
Let's enjoy Paris. It's Valentine's Day.

464
00:17:43,180 --> 00:17:43,880
走吧
Come on.

465
00:17:43,916 --> 00:17:46,274
你这身帅气衣服是哪里弄来的
Where did you get this crazy get-up?

466
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:47,340
人家会盯着我们看的啦
People are gonna stare.

467
00:17:49,760 --> 00:17:52,960
机器人博物馆中你最喜欢的是哪一部分
So...what was your favorite part of the robot museum?

468
00:17:53,160 --> 00:17:53,860
我的妈呀
Oh, man.

469
00:17:54,080 --> 00:17:55,779
太难选了 你先说
I can't decide. You go first.

470
00:17:55,779 --> 00:17:57,238
我说完你就会抄我的
No, you'll just copy me.

471
00:17:57,437 --> 00:17:58,411
我的确会
I'll do that.

472
00:17:59,670 --> 00:18:02,420
那我们就同时间一起说吧
Well, let's, uh, let's just say it at the same time.

473
00:18:02,420 --> 00:18:03,260
数到三
On three.

474
00:18:03,560 --> 00:18:05,400
一 二 三
One, two, three.

475
00:18:05,400 --> 00:18:06,976
-机械猴子乐队 -机械猴子乐队
- The mechanical monkey band. - The mechanical monkey band.

476
00:18:06,976 --> 00:18:07,998
-异口同声 -异口同声
- Le jinx! - Jinx!

477
00:18:08,770 --> 00:18:10,158
双重异口同声
Double jinx.

478
00:18:12,605 --> 00:18:13,635
给两位
Pour vous deux.

479
00:18:13,635 --> 00:18:16,420
天啊 是一幅画
O-Oh, my God. It's a painting!

480
00:18:16,420 --> 00:18:17,780
画了我们
Of us!

481
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:19,640
谢谢
Merci.

482
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:21,594
-谢谢 -谢啦
- Merci beaucoup. - Merci.

483
00:18:22,389 --> 00:18:24,334
我的手是不是搭着你的手
Is my...hand on yours?

484
00:18:24,334 --> 00:18:27,064
是啊 但是... 我们没有这么做吧
Yeah, but I-I don't... think we did that.

485
00:18:29,085 --> 00:18:32,591
这个... 我是时候回去找克莱尔了
Well, um, I better -- better go find Claire.

486
00:18:32,840 --> 00:18:33,397
当然啦 是的
Of course. Yes.

487
00:18:33,397 --> 00:18:35,635
感觉怪怪的 但我们是时候说再见了
Okay. W-Weird. I guess this is goodbye.

488
00:18:35,635 --> 00:18:37,529
这个... 这个你拿去吧
You -- You should have this.

489
00:18:37,540 --> 00:18:38,240
你收着吧
Keep it.

490
00:18:39,240 --> 00:18:41,060
30年后再拿来给我
You'll give it to me in 30 years.

491
00:18:41,720 --> 00:18:42,300
在约定的咖啡店相会
In our cafe.

492
00:18:43,320 --> 00:18:44,420
我一定到
I'll be there.

493
00:18:46,831 --> 00:18:49,461
再会了 基
Au revoir... Guy.

494
00:18:57,860 --> 00:18:59,060
我问了歌洛莉亚
I talked to Gloria.

495
00:18:59,660 --> 00:19:01,100
就觉得能在这里找到你
Thought I might find you here.

496
00:19:01,100 --> 00:19:04,340
太可惜了 圣母院
It's a shame, Notre Dame.

497
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:06,240
那场大火
The fire.

498
00:19:07,220 --> 00:19:07,780
是啊
Yeah.

499
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:10,740
想当年它是多么了不起啊
It used to be so impressive back in its day.

500
00:19:10,796 --> 00:19:12,728
现在也还是很了不起啊
It's still pretty impressive.

501
00:19:13,660 --> 00:19:15,420
空有壳而没有灵魂了
Just a shell of its former self.

502
00:19:16,760 --> 00:19:18,660
最好的年头已随火而去
Best days are behind it.

503
00:19:20,060 --> 00:19:21,780
再也回不到从前了
It'll never be the same.

504
00:19:23,998 --> 00:19:27,927
虽然经受一些风雨 但它还是屹立不摇啊
It's taken some hits, but it's still standing,

505
00:19:28,151 --> 00:19:30,217
而那... 可是勇气与毅力
and that's -- that's grit.

506
00:19:30,400 --> 00:19:32,240
也正是那种精神激励了人们
That's what inspires people.

507
00:19:32,820 --> 00:19:34,640
我也被这精神所激励
That's what inspires me.

508
00:19:35,560 --> 00:19:36,920
真的是丢死人了
It's so embarrassing.

509
00:19:37,760 --> 00:19:39,360
一大家子大老远跑来
The whole reason the family's here

510
00:19:39,360 --> 00:19:41,080
就是为了见证我拿到那个破奖
is to see me get that damn award.

511
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:41,880
老爸
Oh, Dad!

512
00:19:42,120 --> 00:19:44,760
整个家族里 只有我跟你在乎衣柜
You and I are the only ones in this family who care about closets.

513
00:19:45,244 --> 00:19:47,787
大家会来 是因为我们都爱你
We're here because we love you.

514
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:49,260
来嘛
Come on.

515
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:50,720
一起去准备好吃这顿晚饭吧
Let's go get ready for that dinner.

516
00:19:57,820 --> 00:20:00,660
在一个行业中奋斗45年是很长的一段时间
45 years is a long time to spend in one industry,

517
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:02,580
我也达成过许多成就
and I've accomplished a lot.

518
00:20:03,120 --> 00:20:06,240
静声铰链为全美无数的卧室带来宁静
The whisper hinge brought serenity to the American bedroom.

519
00:20:06,560 --> 00:20:10,380
我的发光门把为黑暗中更衣掀起革命
My glow knobs revolutionized getting dressed in the dark.

520
00:20:10,380 --> 00:20:11,920
我还领衔主导了
And I led the charge

521
00:20:11,920 --> 00:20:15,140
鞋架倾斜角度的标准制定
to standardize the angle of shoe racks.

522
00:20:15,244 --> 00:20:17,565
不过我一生中最让我感到自豪的...
But the thing that I'm -- that I'm proudest of...

523
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:20,380
是我的家庭
is my family.

524
00:20:21,620 --> 00:20:23,680
谢谢你们陪我来
Thank you for being here.

525
00:20:24,300 --> 00:20:25,400
我爱你们大家
I love you all.

526
00:20:27,820 --> 00:20:29,840
你们就是我的终身成就奖
You're my lifetime achievement award.

527
00:20:30,055 --> 00:20:32,600
-谢谢你 老爸 -谢谢你的夸奖
- Oh! Thanks, Dad. - That's so sweet.

528
00:20:32,600 --> 00:20:33,660
我们也爱你
We love you, too.

529
00:20:33,734 --> 00:20:35,021
我们爱你 杰
We love you, Jay.

530
00:20:35,021 --> 00:20:37,063
克莱尔·普里契特
Claire Pritchett?

531
00:20:37,935 --> 00:20:40,140
让·卢克
Jean-Luc?!

532
00:20:40,140 --> 00:20:42,400
我大学在这里时过得十分逍遥啊
I had a lot of fun here in college.

533
00:20:42,820 --> 00:20:44,320
你怎么在这里
What are you doing here?

534
00:20:45,370 --> 00:20:46,491
这是我丈夫
This is my husband.
